### 1. Login as customer
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 2. Who am I (should return the customer)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me

### 3. Wrong password (expect 401)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@test.com",
  "password": "wrong"
}

### 4. Register with an email that already exists (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "email": "customer@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 5. Register a new user (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New User",
  "email": "new@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 6. Logout (expect 200)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/logout

### 7. Who am I after logout (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/auth/me

### 8. Login as agent
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agent@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 9. Login as customer again
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 10. Customer lists tickets (expect only the 2 of this customer)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/tickets

### 11. Customer opens a ticket of another customer (expect 403)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/3

### 12. Customer views own ticket with comments (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/2

### 13. Create a ticket (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Projector not working in room 101",
  "description": "The lecture hall projector shows no signal.",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "medium"
}

### 14. Create with invalid data (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "Missing title",
  "category": "Hardware",
  "priority": "urgent"
}

### 15. Edit own ticket (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "University email not working",
  "description": "Still getting invalid password after the reset.",
  "category": "Account access",
  "priority": "high"
}

### 16. FORBIDDEN ACTION: customer tries to delete (expect 403)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/1

### 17. Login as agent
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agent@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 18. Agent lists all tickets (expect every ticket)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/tickets

### 19. Agent changes status (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "in_progress"
}

### 20. Agent deletes a ticket (expect 200)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/4

### 21. Delete a ticket that does not exist (expect 404)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/999

### 22. Login as customer
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 23. Add a comment to own ticket (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/2/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "The problem is still there this morning."
}

### 24. Comment on another customer's ticket (expect 403)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/3/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "I should not be able to write this."
}

### 25. Empty comment (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/tickets/2/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": ""
}

### 26. Edit own comment (expect 200)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/comments/2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Thanks, it happened again today at 14:00 and 16:30."
}

### 27. Edit the agent's comment (expect 403)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/comments/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "body": "Changed by a customer."
}

### 28. Customer deletes the agent's comment (expect 403)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/comments/1

### 29. Login as agent
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "agent@test.com",
  "password": "Test1234!"
}

### 30. Agent deletes a customer comment (expect 200)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/comments/2

### 31. Delete a comment that does not exist (expect 404)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/comments/999 

### 32. Unknown route (expect 404 with a JSON error)
GET http://localhost:3000/api/nothing-here

### 33. Broken JSON body (expect 400 with a JSON error)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "customer@test.com", 